change the window width it adjust itself correctly.\n\nIn this example it seems to resize correctly if the window size is getting bigger but not when it's getting smaller (or only rarely or sometimes when changing very fast).\nIn my real app it doesn't resize in either way but I can't reproduce it into a small example.\n\nI couldn't get this behavior on jsfiddle or codepen but here is an example html page:\n\n``` html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"de\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>Chart Test</title>\n    <style>\n        html, body {\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            margin: 0;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div style=\"width:100%;height:60%\">\n      <canvas id=\"myChart\" style=\"width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background-color:#ddd;height:40%;\">\n      Lower Container\n    </div>\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/Chart.js/2.2.1/Chart.min.js\"></script>\n    <script>\n        window.onload = function() {\n            var ctx = document.getElementById(\"myChart\").getContext(\"2d\");\n            var data = {\n              labels: [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\", \"F\", \"G\"],\n              datasets: [{\n                label: \"Test\",\n                data: [65, 59, 80, 81, 56, 55, 40],\n              }]\n            };\n            var myLineChart = new Chart(ctx, {\n              type: 'line',\n              data: data,\n              options: {\n                maintainAspectRatio: false\n              }\n            });\n        }\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"simonbrunel","id":3874900,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NzQ5MDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3874900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonbrunel","html_url":"https://github.com/simonbrunel","followers_url":"